{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TJgE1R7w6fbAiThNuGRtDL","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\tEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Title\n7\tOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n8\t(Note: \"Guaranteed\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \"Near-Complete\" is honest and defensible.)\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\tLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n12\t\n13\t**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n14\t- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n15\t- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n16\t- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n17\t- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n18\t\n19\t## Core Claims\n20\t\n21\t### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\n22\tLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n23\t\n24\t**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n25\t\n26\t**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n27\t\n28\t**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n29\t\n30\t### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\n31\tSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n32\t- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n33\t- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n34\t- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n35\t\n36\t**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n37\t\n38\t### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\n39\tOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n40\t1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n41\t2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n42\t\n43\tThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n44\t\n45\tThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n46\t\n47\t**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\n48\tWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n49\t\n50\t**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n51\t- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n52\t- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n53\t- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n54\t- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n55\t\n56\t**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n57\t\n58\t**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n59\t\n60\t**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n61\t- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n62\t- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n63\t- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n64\t\n65\t### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n66\t- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n67\t- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n68\t\n69\t**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n70\t\n71\t⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n72\t\n73\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n74\t\n75\t### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n76\t**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n77\t\n78\t### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n79\t**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n80\t\n81\tPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n82\t\n83\t**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n84\t1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n85\t2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n86\t3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n87\t4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n88\t\n89\t数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n90\t\n91\t**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n92\t5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n93\t6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n94\t7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n95\t\n96\t### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n97\t**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n98\t\n99\t### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n100\t**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n101\t\n102\t**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n103\t\n104\t### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n105\t**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE. Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n106\t- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), F1-neutral (-0.14pp)\n107\t- DocRED unconstrained: DR 26.15%, RV 16.03%, R-F1 5.98% (parse failures 6.8% vs Qwen 1.2%)\n108\t- DocRED full_s1: 🔄 ETA ~20:19 UTC\n109\t\n110\t**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n111\t- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n112\t- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n113\t- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n114\t- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n115\t- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n116\t- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n117\t\n118\t### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n119\t**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **D012 Bootstrap CI (10000×, v2 fix) 结果**:\n120\t- SciERC: Rel F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58), Ent F1 -0.03pp (p=0.53) → **F1-neutral**\n121\t- DocRED: Rel F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001, CI [+0.23, +0.81]), Ent F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001, CI [+0.94, +1.55]) → **双双显著提升**\n122\t- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n123\t- Frame as: \"Constraint enforcement preserves or improves extraction quality: F1-neutral on SciERC; statistically significant Rel F1 and Entity F1 improvement on DocRED (p<0.001).\"\n124\t- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告 significance + 机制归因。Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\n125\t\n126\t### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n127\t**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n128\t\n129\t**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n130\t- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n131\t- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n132\t- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n133\t\n134\t**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n135\t\n136\t**论证层次**：\n137\t1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n138\t2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n139\t3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n140\t4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n141\t\n142\t**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n143\t\n144\t**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n145\t\n146\t**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n147\t\n148\t### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n149\t**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n150\t\n151\t## Paper Structure (Draft)\n152\t1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n153\t2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n154\t3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n155\t4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n156\t5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n157\t6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n158\t7. Conclusion\n159\t\n160\t## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n161\t\n162\t**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n163\t- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n164\t- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n165\t- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n166\t- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n167\t- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n168\t\n169\t**Claim with caution**:\n170\t- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n171\t- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n172\t- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n173\t- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n174\t\n175\t**Do NOT claim**:\n176\t- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n177\t- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n178\t- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n179\t- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n180\t- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n181\t- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n182\t- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n183\t\n184\t## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n185\t\n186\t1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n187\t2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n188\t3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n189\t4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n190\t5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n191\t\n192\t## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n193\t\n194\t- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n195\t- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n196\t- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED 2 组实验 ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc baseline ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n197\t- **May 14-15**: D014 tightness claim 修订 + §5 cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion 修正 (Agent 执行中)\n198\t- **May 15-17**: 全文校对 + Discussion 整合 + 最终数字确认\n199\t- **May 19**: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n200\t- **May 19-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n201\t\n202\t**当前瓶颈**: D014 论文修订（tightness claim + cross-model subsection + E-F1 claim limitation）\n203\t\n204\t## Status\n205\t- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n206\t- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n207\t- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n208\t- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n209\t- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n210\t- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n211\t- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n212\t- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n213\t- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n214\t- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n215\t- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n216\t- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n217\t- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n218\t- D014 tightness revision: 🔄 Agent executing (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n219\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dfc5dc4-a95d-4cb7-b790-c6ab597d3a86","uuid":"ab251013-57b4-4025-9407-a096841465c5","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:14:02.075Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T205155/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# OntoCoDec — Paper Framing\n\n## Target Venue\nEMNLP 2026 (ARR submission May 25, 2026)\n\n## Title\nOntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction via Compiled Ontology Constraints\n(Note: \"Guaranteed\" dropped per Reviewer — S1 DR=0.93%, S2 DR=0.97%, neither achieves 0%. \"Near-Complete\" is honest and defensible.)\n\n## Core Insight\nLLM-based IE systems produce systematic ontology constraint violations concentrated in specific relation types. Prompt-level intervention (schema-informed prompting) reduces violations by ~62% but cannot eliminate them — certain relation types retain 25-30% violation rates even with explicit constraint descriptions. OntoCoDec provides **near-complete elimination (DR 15.4%→0.93%, ↓94%) at zero or positive F1 impact** through automatic ontology-to-decoder constraint compilation with two complementary layers.\n\n**Phase 2 confirmed (D012 bootstrap CI, v2 fix)**: Grammar+Semantic dual-layer constrained decoding reduces domain/range violations by 94%, eliminates entity-type and relation-vocabulary violations entirely (→0%). F1 impact is **dataset-dependent**:\n- SciERC: Rel F1 neutral (+0.13pp, p=0.58), Ent F1 neutral (-0.03pp, p=0.53)\n- DocRED: Rel F1 **significantly improved** (+0.50pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.23, +0.81]); Ent F1 **significantly improved** (+1.23pp, p<0.001, 95% CI [+0.94, +1.55])\n- Mechanism: grammar 消除 OOV relation names (DocRED RV 29.66%→0.03%) + 非标 entity types (ET 2.48%→0%)。all_set F1 方法下 OOV=FP → fewer FP → higher precision/F1。SciERC baseline RV/ET 已很低，效果不显著。\n- **Grammar 层是 F1 提升的唯一来源**: grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37% (Δ+0.01pp, p=0.66)。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献，专注 DR reduction。\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### Claim 1 (Empirical): Violation Landscape\nLLM-based IE systems violate ontology type constraints at non-trivial rates (15.4% per-triple on SciERC, 18.7% on DocRED). Violations are **not uniformly distributed** — they concentrate on relation types with tight domain/range constraints (Feature-of 33.5%, Compare 42.4%) while loose-constraint relations show near-zero violation (Used-for 0.8%).\n\n**Key insight**: Violation rate is driven by **constraint tightness**, not ontology size. A small ontology with tight constraints can produce more violations than a large ontology with loose constraints.\n\n**D014 修订**: DR reduction ceiling 由 **tightness × model RV baseline** 共同决定，非 tightness 单因素。Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% vs Qwen DR↓44.7%（同一 ontology τ̄=0.842）。机制：Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 层将 OOV triples 强制匹配有效关系名 → 揭露大量 latent DR violations → 残余 DR 更高。这是比单一 tightness 更深的 insight。\n\n**Evidence**: SciERC (7 relations) 15.4%; DocRED (96 relations) 18.7% — comparable rates despite 14× ontology size difference. Schema-informed prompt on DocRED only achieves DR↓32% (vs SciERC ↓62%), confirming **prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity**.\n\n### Claim 2 (Empirical): Prompt Insufficiency\nSchema-informed prompting (explicitly describing domain/range constraints in the prompt) reduces but does not eliminate violations:\n- Overall: 15.4% → 5.78% (-62.4%), still above 5%\n- Per-relation: Compare 42.4% → 27.6%, Evaluate-for 24.1% → 29.9% (**worse**)\n- Prompt intervention is unreliable at the per-relation level — some relations improve, one regresses\n\n**Narrative**: This is NOT about \"5.78% barely above 5%\". The story is: **prompt-level intervention is fundamentally unreliable as a guarantee mechanism**. It works statistically but cannot provide per-instance compliance. Three specific relation types retain >10% violation rates with schema-informed prompts. For safety-critical IE (biomedical, legal, regulatory), statistical reduction is insufficient — guaranteed compliance is required.\n\n### Claim 3 (Methodological): Composable Constraint Framework\nOntoCoDec automatically compiles IE ontology schemas into two composable constraint layers:\n1. **Grammar layer** (XGrammar): JSON structure + type vocabulary constraints (CFG-expressible)\n2. **Semantic layer** (TypeConstraintProcessor): Cross-field domain/range constraints via stateful entity registry + dynamic logit masking\n\nThe two layers are **complementary with enabling dependency**: grammar ensures every generated relation type is in the valid vocabulary, which enables the semantic layer to look up and enforce domain/range rules for that type. Without grammar, the semantic layer encounters unknown relation types and cannot enforce constraints (explaining why semantic_only achieves only ↓24% vs full_s1 ↓94%). This is NOT \"synergistic\" (mutual amplification) — grammar is a prerequisite for semantic, not vice versa.\n\nThe two layers compose via bitwise AND of token masks. Recommended framing: \"Grammar and semantic constraints compose via bitwise AND with an enabling dependency: grammar ensures structural validity, enabling semantic constraints to enforce domain/range rules. When constraint tightness creates empty intersection between layers, the system degrades gracefully to grammar-only constraints, maintaining structural validity as a guaranteed floor.\"\n\n**Graceful degradation + Fallback 频率量化** (D008 + Reviewer 发现):\nWhen $M_{semantic} \\cap M_{grammar} = \\emptyset$, the system falls back to grammar-only control.\n\n**关键量化数据（Reviewer 从日志挖掘）**:\n- Llama DocRED full_s1: **32,921 次 fallback / 577 docs = ~57 次/doc**\n- Llama SciERC full_s1: **5,882 次 fallback / 550 docs = ~10.7 次/doc**\n- DocRED fallback 频率是 SciERC 的 **5.3×**\n- Qwen DocRED fallback 率未知（日志当时无 fallback logging，需估算）\n\n**这直接解释了 DocRED DR 残余 10.19% vs SciERC 0.93%**: 更多 token 位置退化为 grammar-only → grammar-only 的 DR 已知为 26.17% → 高 fallback = 高残余 DR。\n\n**论文建议**: 在 §5 tightness 段报告 fallback 率，定义 \"Constraint Coverage\" 指标（semantic masking 实际生效的 token 比例）。这把 \"10.19% DR 残余\" 从弱点变成可量化分析的 finding。Frame as \"engineering robustness\" in §4; fallback 频率 + tightness 作为 §5 定量分析。\n\n**Decidability taxonomy**: Constraints classified by prefix-decidability:\n- (a) Purely local: entity type ∈ vocabulary (grammar layer)\n- (b) Prefix-decidable with state: relation argument types compatible with domain/range (semantic layer, requires entity registry)\n- (c) Truly non-local: forward coreference — out of scope for forward-only decoding\n\n### Claim 4 (Methodological): S1 vs S2 Decoding Strategies — Architectural Ablation\n- S1 (single-pass): Both layers applied throughout generation. **Recommended primary strategy** — simpler, slightly better metrics across the board.\n- S2 (two-pass): Pass 1 extracts entities (grammar-only), Pass 2 generates relations with input-dependent grammar compiled from Pass 1 entities.\n\n**S2 full results (551/551 SciERC)**: DR 0.97% (vs S1 0.93%), CF 8.03% (vs S1 9.9%), R-F1 8.03% (vs S1 8.36%). S2 does NOT solve CF — the 1.87pp reduction is not significant. S2 also slightly worse on DR and F1. **S2 is an architectural variant demonstrating framework flexibility, not a CF solution.** Position in paper as ablation (Section 5 or Appendix), not as a core contribution.\n\n⚠️ **Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence** — small-sample artifact; full run shows DR=0.97%. Per-relation S2 DR is worse than S1 on Compare (4.6% vs 2.82%), Part-of (1.25% vs 0%), Used-for (0.12% vs 0%).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### C1: \"5.78% is barely above 5% — threshold is arbitrary\"\n**Response**: Don't argue about the threshold. Argue about per-relation distribution: Compare (27.6%), Evaluate-for (29.9%), Feature-of (11.3%) have double-digit violation rates with schema-informed prompt. The value proposition is per-relation guaranteed compliance, not overall statistical rate.\n\n### C2: \"Why not just post-hoc filter?\"\n**Response (D013, 实验结果已出)**:\n\nPost-hoc filtering 实验结果：post-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36, DocRED 9.61 vs 8.24）——因 low F1 regime 下移除 FP 大幅提升 precision。\n\n**论文 framing（不以 F1 论高低，多维对比）**:\n1. **Recall 维度（核心论点）**: OntoCoDec recall 上升 (SciERC +0.20pp, DocRED +0.56pp) = 概率质量重分配到合法 token 生效。Post-hoc recall 下降 (SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp) = 正确 triple 被误删。\n2. **Information coverage**: DocRED post-hoc 丢弃 **48.1%** triples（近半数信息丢失），SciERC 16.8%。OntoCoDec 保留全部 triple slots。\n3. **Operational**: OntoCoDec 产出即合规、无需后处理、支持流式。Post-hoc 需额外管线、不适用实时场景。\n4. **Precision trade-off（诚实承认）**: \"Post-hoc achieves higher precision by removing a large fraction of triples, many of which are incorrect. This trades information coverage for precision — valid when FP are costly, but inadequate when completeness matters.\"\n\n数据表：SciERC post-hoc rejection 16.8%, OntoCoDec recall 11.60 vs post-hoc 10.68; DocRED post-hoc rejection 48.1%, OntoCoDec recall 10.02 vs post-hoc 8.40。\n\n**Reviewer 补充发现（D013 后）**:\n5. **ET 残余**：post-hoc 只删 triples 不改 entity list，残余 ET=0.4% (SciERC) / 2.47% (DocRED)。OntoCoDec ET=0%。Post-hoc 无法解决 entity type 违规。\n6. **127 个被删 TP (DocRED)**：过滤前 TP=1137，过滤后 TP=1010。丢失的 127 个 TP（11.2%）是正确提取但 entity type 违规的 triple。OntoCoDec 通过生成时强制合法 type 保留这些 TP——\"prevent vs detect\" 核心论据的具体数据。\n7. **OntoCoDec+post-hoc 组合**（future work idea）：先 constrain 再 filter 残余 DR。低优先级，May 19 前不做。\n\n### C3: \"Bitwise AND of two masks is not novel\"\n**Response**: The novelty is not the AND operation — it's (a) the automatic compilation from ontology definitions (zero-code schema compliance), (b) the stateful entity registry enabling cross-field constraints during autoregressive generation, (c) the decidability taxonomy providing theoretical guidance, and (d) the systematic violation landscape measurement motivating the approach.\n\n### C4: \"Evaluate-for violation rate increases with schema-informed prompt\"\n**Response (prior-constraint conflict framework)**: Evaluate-for has 23/36 valid pairs; Method→Task is invalid for Evaluate-for but natural in the LLM's distributional prior (\"Method X evaluates for Task Y\" is semantically plausible). Schema-informed prompting creates a **prior-constraint conflict**: the model learns to avoid Method→Task for Evaluate-for (reducing count 133→87, -34.6%), but the remaining instances are harder boundary cases where the model's type assignment strategy becomes less stable. This is not just \"harder instances\" — it's an active interference between prompt-level constraint signals and the model's learned type associations.\n\n**This strengthens the paper's claim**: prompt-level intervention is not merely insufficient but potentially **counterproductive** for specific constraint configurations. Decoding-time enforcement avoids this issue entirely — it operates on logits, not on the model's reasoning process, so there is no prior-constraint conflict.\n\n### C5: \"Only tested on one model (Qwen3-8B)\"\n**Response**: Cross-model validation DONE. Llama-3.1-8B 零代码修改：\n- SciERC: DR 13.34%→0.08% (↓99.4%), F1-neutral (-0.14pp)\n- DocRED unconstrained: DR 26.15%, RV 16.03%, R-F1 5.98% (parse failures 6.8% vs Qwen 1.2%)\n- DocRED full_s1: 🔄 ETA ~20:19 UTC\n\n**Cross-model claim 指导（Reviewer 专项评估）**:\n- ✅ 可声明：\"OntoCoDec generalizes across model families without code modification\"（程序性事实，铁证）\n- ❌ 不可声明：\"consistently achieves the same reduction rate\"（仅 2 模型，不足以量化声明）\n- **RV↓DR↑ 正交性 finding**: Llama RV baseline 低(16%) 但 DR baseline 高(26%)，反向于 Qwen。证明两层约束解决正交 failure modes——vocabulary compliance ≠ semantic compliance。应作为 §5 cross-model 独立 finding 展开。\n- **Parse failure 偏差**: checker skip parse failures (不计入 F1)，Llama 68/998=6.8% vs Qwen 12/998=1.2%。偏差方向保守（不利于 constrained），不威胁 claim。但需 footnote 披露 + cross-model 表增加 parse failure rate 行。\n- **Llama SciERC CF=6.56%**: 比 Qwen 同量级更高，non-local constraint 问题在 Llama 上更突出，limitations 提及。\n- 等 llama_docred_full_s1 出来后定最终 claim 措辞。\n\n### C6: \"Constrained decoding degrades generation quality (CRANE, Structure Snowballing)\"\n**Response**: OntoCoDec's semantic constraints are narrower than full grammar constraints — only type tokens are masked, free text is unconstrained. **D012 Bootstrap CI (10000×, v2 fix) 结果**:\n- SciERC: Rel F1 +0.13pp (p=0.58), Ent F1 -0.03pp (p=0.53) → **F1-neutral**\n- DocRED: Rel F1 +0.50pp (p<0.001, CI [+0.23, +0.81]), Ent F1 +1.23pp (p<0.001, CI [+0.94, +1.55]) → **双双显著提升**\n- 机制：grammar 消除 OOV relation names + 非标 entity types → all_set 方法下减少 FP → precision 提升。Grammar 是 F1 提升的唯一来源（grammar_only Ent F1=59.38% ≈ full_s1 59.37%, Δ=0.01pp, p=0.66）。Semantic 层对 F1 无额外贡献。\n- Frame as: \"Constraint enforcement preserves or improves extraction quality: F1-neutral on SciERC; statistically significant Rel F1 and Entity F1 improvement on DocRED (p<0.001).\"\n- 不升级为 core claim，但如实报告 significance + 机制归因。Note: S2 shows marginally lower F1 and fewer triples (1644 vs 1729) — two-pass does not improve quality.\n\n### C7: \"Your method trades DR violations for CF violations (cross-field consistency)\"\n**Response**: Both S1 and S2 show elevated CF (per-triple rate ~8-10%). This is an inherent limitation of per-relation independent type enforcement. Must be proactively reported as a limitation. Defense:\n\n**CF 子类型分析（根因已确认）**：\n- **EVR（entity-vs-relation type drift）**: 占 CF 的 >90%。同一 entity 在 entity list 和 relation triple 中被赋予不同 type。S1: 245 entities (7.34%), S2: 178 entities (5.54%, -27%)\n- **Within-rel（同 entity 跨 relation type 不一致）**: S1: 10 (0.36%), S2: 18 (0.72%)\n- S2 减少 EVR 但增加 within-rel——trade-off 更复杂，不是单纯好/差\n\n**Top 冲突模式**: Generic↔OtherScientificTerm (60次), Material↔OtherScientificTerm (28次), Material↔Method (20次)。**这些是 SciERC type system 固有的语义边界模糊区**——同一术语在不同学术语境下确实可以被合理归类为不同 type。CF 在相当程度上是 type system 模糊性的体现，非纯粹的方法缺陷。\n\n**论证层次**：\n1. DR violations = structurally invalid triples（下游系统不可用）→ hard constraint\n2. CF violations = same entity gets different types across relations → individual triples remain type-valid, only cross-triple consistency broken → soft preference\n3. CF 的根因是 type system 语义边界模糊 + per-relation 独立 enforcement，非 bug\n4. Future work: cross-relation global consistency pass (entity-level type consensus before relation-specific enforcement)\n\n**机制归因（口径对账确认）**：grammar_only CF=0.08%（与 unconstrained 持平），full_s1 CF=9.90%，full_s2 CF=8.03%。**CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入，grammar 层无贡献。** 这为 \"CF 是 semantic type enforcement 的系统性副作用\" 提供干净的消融证据。\n\n**论文数字口径**：CF rate 用 violation_checker 口径（denominator=total_entities，与 DR/RV/ET 一致）。分析段落额外给 entity-level EVR 率 + 受影响样本比例。注意：analyze_cf 脚本的 EVR/WR 两维度不是独立的（WR⊂EVR），论文中不要作为两个独立维度报告。\n\n**Do NOT hide this data.** Proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis + type ambiguity evidence + 消融归因 = 最强防御策略。\n\n### C8: \"Absolute F1 is too low (~8%) — results are not meaningful\"\n**Response**: This is a zero-shot extraction setting (no training data, no fine-tuning). Low F1 is expected — supervised SOTA on SciERC relation F1 is ~40-50%. Our contribution is the constraint enforcement method, not extraction quality. F1 is a control variable verifying constraints don't degrade quality, not an optimization target. Recommended framing: \"We evaluate in a zero-shot setting to demonstrate that our constraint enforcement method works without task-specific training. F1 is reported to verify that constraint enforcement does not degrade extraction quality, not as a claim of state-of-the-art performance.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (Draft)\n1. Introduction: Violation landscape motivation + composable constraint framework overview\n2. Background: Grammar-constrained decoding (XGrammar) + IE ontology structure\n3. Violation Landscape Study (Phase 0 empirics — independent contribution)\n4. OntoCoDec Framework: Compiler + TypeConstraintProcessor + S1/S2 strategies\n5. Experiments: Constrained vs unconstrained vs post-hoc vs prompt-based\n6. Related Work: 5 constraint paradigms (grammar, vocabulary, structural, type-checking, ontology)\n7. Conclusion\n\n## Claim Calibration (per Reviewer assessment)\n\n**Safe to claim (sufficient evidence from Phase 2)**:\n- \"First systematic study of ontology constraint violations in LLM-based IE\"\n- \"Violation rate correlates with constraint tightness, not ontology size\" (D014: DR reduction ceiling 由 tightness × model RV baseline 共同决定)\n- \"Grammar+semantic constrained decoding eliminates 94% of DR violations at zero F1 cost\" ✅ Phase 2 confirmed\n- \"Two-layer architecture provides complementary coverage — grammar enables semantic\" ✅ Ablation confirmed\n- \"Prompt-level intervention scales poorly with ontology complexity\" ✅ SciERC ↓62% vs DocRED ↓32%\n\n**Claim with caution**:\n- \"Near-complete type-valid IE\" — S1 0.93%, S2 0.97% residual, not truly 0%. Title updated to \"Near-Complete\"\n- \"Principled framework applicable to arbitrary IE ontologies\" — validated on 2 datasets + 1 model only\n- \"F1 improvement\" — SciERC: not significant (p=0.58), frame as F1-neutral; DocRED: significant (+0.50pp, p<0.001), 可报告但不升级为 core claim，归因于 OOV elimination 而非约束解码本身的提升\n- \"CF reveals type system ambiguity\" — 可在 §5.3 作为 analysis finding 展开（Generic↔OtherScientificTerm 等模式有独立 insight 价值），但 §7 必须同时保留 CF 作为 limitation + future work。**两处都要有，缺一不可。** 不能暗示\"因为是 type ambiguity 所以 CF 可接受\"\n\n**Do NOT claim**:\n- \"General infrastructure for IE\" — only zero-shot extraction validated\n- \"State-of-the-art\" — F1 is control variable, not optimization target (see C8)\n- \"Synergistic effect\" — mechanism is enabling dependency, not mutual amplification (see Claim 3)\n- \"S2 solves CF\" or \"S2 mitigates Structure Snowballing\" — data shows S2 ≈ S1 on all metrics; position as architectural variant only\n- \"Pilot50 DR=0%\" — small-sample artifact, full S2 has DR=0.97%\n- \"Grammar-first invariant\" 作为独立 claim — 证据不足（仅 1 次崩溃触发，实现是 fallback 非形式化保证）。写入 §4 方法论设计原则（1-2 句），不升级为 claim\n- \"Robust dual-layer composition across schema complexities\" — 等 DocRED 完成。最终如 fallback ≤5/998，可写经验性陈述，不做泛化 claim\n\n## Risk Ranking (ordered by reject probability)\n\n1. **CF violation trade-off under-addressed** (MEDIUM-HIGH): S1 9.9%, S2 8.03% — both elevated. **S2 confirmed: does NOT solve CF.** This is the #1 attack surface. Mitigated by proactive disclosure + severity distinction + root cause analysis (C7). Must be reported as explicit limitation with future work direction (global entity-type consensus).\n2. ~~**Single model limitation**~~ (RESOLVED): Llama-3.1-8B SciERC ✅ (DR↓99.4%) + DocRED ✅ (DR↓90.2%). 2 模型 × 2 数据集全矩阵完成。\n3. **Novelty perception** (MEDIUM): \"PLDI'25 for code → OntoCoDec for IE\" attack line. Must argue IE constraint structure differs fundamentally.\n4. ~~**DocRED Phase 2 weak**~~ (RESOLVED → reframed as D014): Qwen DR↓44.7%, Llama DR↓90.2% — both substantial. Weaker Qwen reduction explained by RV baseline interaction (D014), not method failure.\n5. ~~**Phase 2 F1 drop**~~ (RESOLVED): F1 confirmed neutral (SciERC) or positive (DocRED, p<0.001). Bootstrap CI D012 confirms. No longer a risk.\n\n## Critical Path to EMNLP Submission (May 25)\n\n- **May 13-14**: Phase 0 + Phase 1 + Phase 2 SciERC ✅\n- **May 14**: Phase 2 DocRED 4-way ablation ✅ + Llama SciERC cross-model ✅ + Dream 完成 (3/6)\n- **May 14-15**: Llama DocRED 2 组实验 ✅ + Checker 修正 ✅ + post-hoc baseline ✅ + bootstrap CI ✅ + related work ✅\n- **May 14-15**: D014 tightness claim 修订 + §5 cross-model subsection + abstract/conclusion 修正 (Agent 执行中)\n- **May 15-17**: 全文校对 + Discussion 整合 + 最终数字确认\n- **May 19**: 内部稿 → submit_paper_to_review\n- **May 19-24**: Review 修改 + 最终提交\n\n**当前瓶颈**: D014 论文修订（tightness claim + cross-model subsection + E-F1 claim limitation）\n\n## Status\n- Phase 0 SciERC: ✅ Complete (minimal + schema-informed)\n- Phase 0 DocRED: ✅ Complete (minimal 18.7% DR + schema-informed 12.8% DR)\n- Phase 1 Compiler: ✅ Complete (grammar + semantic layers integrated)\n- Phase 2 SciERC (5 configs): ✅ Complete (S1 DR↓94% F1-neutral, S2 降级为 ablation)\n- Phase 2 DocRED (4 configs): ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓45%, grammar ET/RV→0%)\n- Llama SciERC cross-model: ✅ Complete (DR↓99.4%, F1-neutral, 零代码修改)\n- Llama DocRED cross-model: ✅ Complete (full_s1 DR↓90.2%, unconstrained DR=26.07%)\n- Checker v2 (D011): ✅ Fixed (ET triple-counting → unique entity dedup)\n- Bootstrap CI (D012): ✅ Fixed + confirmed (entity filter bug resolved)\n- Post-hoc baseline (D013): ✅ Complete (multi-dimensional framing)\n- Related work: ✅ 42 bib entries, 4 additions merged\n- Dream 6/6 actions: ✅ All complete\n- CF violation analysis: ✅ Confirmed inherent limitation (S1 9.9% SciERC / 2.57% DocRED / 12.02% Llama DocRED)\n- D014 tightness revision: 🔄 Agent executing (tightness × RV baseline dual-factor)\n","numLines":219,"startLine":1,"totalLines":219}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MxQhewUWe5dY7h7yLuNZPT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B zero-shot SciERC extraction，minimal prompt，测量 baseline violation rates。 7 relations, 551 abstracts。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"total_triples\": 1724,\n7\t      \"total_entities\": 2474,\n8\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 1.0,\n9\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n10\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0139,\n11\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1537,\n12\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n13\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.3101,\n14\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0823,\n15\t      \"per_relation_dr_top3\": {\n16\t        \"Compare\": 0.4242,\n17\t        \"Feature-of\": 0.3354,\n18\t        \"Part-of\": 0.25\n19\t      },\n20\t      \"per_relation_dr_bottom2\": {\n21\t        \"Used-for\": 0.0076,\n22\t        \"Conjunction\": 0.0\n23\t      }\n24\t    },\n25\t    \"tables\": [\n26\t      \"Table 1: Per-relation DR violation rates (SciERC, minimal prompt). 7 relations ranked by tightness τ.\"\n27\t    ],\n28\t    \"figures\": [],\n29\t    \"analysis\": \"R2 在 median 档会写：\\\"The violation landscape analysis (§3) provides useful empirical grounding, but the causal claim that 'violation rate is driven by tightness' is overstated given confounds (relation frequency, entity type distribution).\\\" 需在 rebuttal 中降级为 correlational + 补充 frequency 作为 covariate 的分析。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，15.4% DR baseline 被 2/3 审稿人接受为 non-trivial。R2 可能质疑： \\\"zero-shot 本身就会产生各种错误，15% constraint violation 在 8% F1 下是否真的重要？\\\" 但 per-relation 分布（Compare 42%、Used-for 0.8%）的极端差异足以说服—— 这不是随机错误，是 constraint tightness 相关的系统性现象。 R1 接受此数据作为 motivation。R3 认为 violation landscape 是独立贡献。\\n\"\n30\t  },\n31\t  {\n32\t    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n33\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B SciERC，schema-informed prompt 将 domain/range constraints 写入 prompt， 测量 prompt-level intervention 效果。\\n\",\n34\t    \"results\": {\n35\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0578,\n36\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.003,\n37\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n38\t      \"total_triples\": 1661,\n39\t      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct\": -62.4,\n40\t      \"per_relation_notable\": {\n41\t        \"Feature-of_delta_pp\": -22.3,\n42\t        \"Part-of_delta_pp\": -22.5,\n43\t        \"Compare_delta_pp\": -14.8,\n44\t        \"Evaluate-for_delta_pp\": 5.8\n45\t      },\n46\t      \"mcnemar_significant\": true\n47\t    },\n48\t    \"tables\": [\n49\t      \"Table 2: Per-relation DR rates under minimal vs. schema-informed prompts, with McNemar test results.\"\n50\t    ],\n51\t    \"figures\": [],\n52\t    \"analysis\": \"Schema-informed prompt 数据在 median 档基本无争议，支撑 Claim 2。 Evaluate-for 回归是一个 talking point 但不构成 major weakness。\\n\\n\\n62.4% reduction 在 median 档被全部审稿人接受为 \\\"substantial but insufficient\\\"。 关键攻击面是 Evaluate-for 回归 (+5.8pp)：R2 会写 \\\"The fact that prompting can *increase* violations for specific relation types (Evaluate-for, §3.2) is an interesting finding but needs more analysis — is this a prior-constraint conflict or simply noise?\\\" Median 档下 R2 对此提出 minor weakness 而非 major，因为论文已有 prior-constraint conflict 解释框架。但 R2 建议 \\\"run significance test on per-relation changes to distinguish real regression from variance.\\\"\\n\"\n53\t  },\n54\t  {\n55\t    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n56\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B DocRED (998 docs, 96 relations)，minimal prompt baseline。\\n\",\n57\t    \"results\": {\n58\t      \"total_docs\": 998,\n59\t      \"parsed_docs\": 962,\n60\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.964,\n61\t      \"total_entities\": 19099,\n62\t      \"total_triples\": 16540,\n63\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.075,\n64\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.289,\n65\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.187,\n66\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n67\t      \"top_dr_by_rate\": {\n68\t        \"P35_head_of_state\": 1.0,\n69\t        \"P710_participant\": 0.919,\n70\t        \"P172_ethnic_group\": 0.875\n71\t      },\n72\t      \"top_dr_by_count\": {\n73\t        \"P31_instance_of\": {\n74\t          \"violations\": 322,\n75\t          \"total\": 533,\n76\t          \"rate\": 0.604\n77\t        },\n78\t        \"P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction\": {\n79\t          \"violations\": 264,\n80\t          \"total\": 594,\n81\t          \"rate\": 0.444\n82\t        }\n83\t      }\n84\t    },\n85\t    \"tables\": [\n86\t      \"Table 1 (extended): DocRED violation rates. Top-10 relations by DR rate and count.\"\n87\t    ],\n88\t    \"figures\": [],\n89\t    \"analysis\": \"RV=28.9% 是 DocRED 特有现象（96 relations 中很多 Qwen 未见过）。 Median R2 会追问 \\\"如果先修 RV 再测 DR，DR 会不会更低？\\\"——恰好引出 grammar_only 实验。\\n\\n\\nDocRED 18.7% DR vs SciERC 15.4%——14× ontology size 差异下 violation rate 相近—— 直接支撑 \\\"violation rate driven by tightness not ontology size\\\" claim。 Median 档下 R1 接受此 finding。R2 会注意到 RV=28.9% 极高，质疑： \\\"Nearly 30% of generated relation names are out-of-vocabulary — how much of DR is confounded by the model simply not knowing the relation names?\\\" 这是 D014 dual-factor insight 的前兆。R2 不会因此 reject 但会要求 disentangle RV 和 DR 的交互效应。\\n\"\n90\t  },\n91\t  {\n92\t    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n93\t    \"description\": \"DocRED schema-informed prompt，测量 prompt-level 在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\\n\",\n94\t    \"results\": {\n95\t      \"total_documents\": 998,\n96\t      \"documents_checked\": 943,\n97\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.9449,\n98\t      \"total_triples\": 16782,\n99\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0061,\n100\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.1841,\n101\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1284,\n102\t      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct\": -31.3\n103\t    },\n104\t    \"tables\": [\n105\t      \"Table 2 (DocRED section): Schema-informed prompt results.\"\n106\t    ],\n107\t    \"figures\": [],\n108\t    \"analysis\": \"Prompt insufficiency claim (C2) 在 median 档获得 3/3 审稿人支持。 这是论文最安全的 claim——数据清晰，叙事直觉合理。\\n\\n\\nDR↓31.3% vs SciERC ↓62.4%——prompt intervention 在复杂 ontology 上效果减半。 Median 档下所有审稿人接受此数据。R2 会标注 \\\"The scaling gap between SciERC (62%) and DocRED (31%) prompt-level reduction is compelling evidence for Claim 2, though confounded by the 96-relation prompt being much longer and potentially overwhelming the model's attention.\\\" 这是 minor point，不构成 major weakness。 R1 认为此数据强化了 decoding-time 方法的 motivation。\\n\"\n109\t  },\n110\t  {\n111\t    \"name\": \"SciERC unconstrained baseline\",\n112\t    \"description\": \"Phase 2 SciERC unconstrained（与 Phase 0 同 pipeline 但 Phase 2 checker v2）， 作为 ablation 的 control condition。\\n\",\n113\t    \"results\": {\n114\t      \"total_samples\": 551,\n115\t      \"total_triples\": 1724,\n116\t      \"total_entities\": 2474,\n117\t      \"json_parse_rate\": 1.0,\n118\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n119\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0139,\n120\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1537,\n121\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n122\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.3101,\n123\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0823\n124\t    },\n125\t    \"tables\": [\n126\t      \"Table 3 row 1: SciERC unconstrained baseline metrics.\"\n127\t    ],\n128\t    \"figures\": [],\n129\t    \"analysis\": \"Baseline 数据确保 ablation 有公平比较基准。F1=8.23% 的 low absolute value 在 median 档下被 R2 提及一次（\\\"results are in very low F1 regime\\\"）但被 zero-shot framing 部分化解（R3 接受，R2 remains skeptical）。\\n\\n\\n与 P001 数值一致（同模型同数据同 prompt，仅 checker 版本更新后数值不变）。 Median 档下此实验本身无争议，仅作为 ablation table 的 row 0。 R2 可能注意到 R-F1=8.23% 绝对值低，引出 C8 concern。\\n\"\n130\t  },\n131\t  {\n132\t    \"name\": \"SciERC grammar-only\",\n133\t    \"description\": \"仅启用 grammar layer (XGrammar CFG)，验证 grammar 层对 violation 的独立效果。\\n\",\n134\t    \"results\": {\n135\t      \"total_triples\": 1725,\n136\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n137\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n138\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1484,\n139\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n140\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.3098,\n141\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0823\n142\t    },\n143\t    \"tables\": [\n144\t      \"Table 3 row 2: SciERC grammar-only.\"\n145\t    ],\n146\t    \"figures\": [],\n147\t    \"analysis\": \"Grammar-only 是 enabling dependency 叙事的关键证据。DR 不降说明 grammar 是 semantic 的 prerequisite 而非 replacement。\\n\\n\\nGrammar 层消除 ET/RV（→0%）但 DR 几乎不变（15.37%→14.84%，Δ-0.53pp）—— 完美演示 grammar 只管 vocabulary 不管 semantics。Median 档下 3/3 审稿人认为 此 ablation 清晰有效。R1 可能评价 \\\"The ablation clearly demonstrates the orthogonal contributions of the two layers — grammar handles vocabulary, semantic handles domain/range.\\\" CF=0.08% 也证明 grammar 层不引入 CF——CF 100% 来自 semantic 层。\\n\"\n148\t  },\n149\t  {\n150\t    \"name\": \"SciERC semantic-only\",\n151\t    \"description\": \"仅启用 semantic layer (TypeConstraintProcessor)，无 grammar 保底。\\n\",\n152\t    \"results\": {\n153\t      \"total_triples\": 1726,\n154\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n155\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0151,\n156\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1165,\n157\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0271,\n158\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.3101,\n159\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0815\n160\t    },\n161\t    \"tables\": [\n162\t      \"Table 3 row 3: SciERC semantic-only.\"\n163\t    ],\n164\t    \"figures\": [],\n165\t    \"analysis\": \"Semantic-only 的 CF=2.71% 已开始上升（unconstrained 0.08%），预示 semantic enforcement 的 CF 副作用。完整 ablation 梯度：unconstrained 0.08% → semantic_only 2.71% → full_s1 9.90%。R1 会注意到此趋势。\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only DR↓24%（vs full_s1 ↓94%）——没有 grammar 保底时 semantic 层遇到 OOV relation types 无法 enforce constraints，效果大打折扣。RV=1.51% 残余证明 semantic 不管 vocabulary。Median 档下此数据被 R1 引用为 \\\"convincing evidence for the enabling dependency between layers.\\\" R2 同意但追问 \\\"What fraction of the 76% gap (24% vs 94%) is due to OOV vs. other failure modes?\\\" 需 rebuttal 补充 OOV relation 占 semantic failure 的比例分析。\\n\"\n166\t  },\n167\t  {\n168\t    \"name\": \"SciERC full S1\",\n169\t    \"description\": \"Grammar + Semantic 双层，single-pass (S1)。论文主推配置。\\n\",\n170\t    \"results\": {\n171\t      \"total_triples\": 1729,\n172\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n173\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n174\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0093,\n175\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.099,\n176\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.3098,\n177\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0836\n178\t    },\n179\t    \"tables\": [\n180\t      \"Table 3 row 4: SciERC full S1 — primary configuration.\",\n181\t      \"Table 4: DR reduction per relation type (unconstrained → S1).\"\n182\t    ],\n183\t    \"figures\": [],\n184\t    \"analysis\": \"Median R1 的 CF major concern 是可回应的：提供 CF 子类型分析（EVR 占 >90%， 根因是 type system 语义模糊），补充 ablation 证明 CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入， 并提出 future work direction（global entity-type consensus）。但需要 rebuttal 中 实际补充这些分析，不能仅靠声明。估计 rebuttal effort 3-4 天。\\n\\n\\nDR=0.93% (↓94%) 是论文最强数据点。Median 档下 R1 和 R3 对 DR 结果高度满意。 但 CF=9.90% 是 #1 攻击面：R1 写 \\\"The method trades DR violations (15.4%→0.93%) for CF violations (0.08%→9.90%). While the authors argue CF is 'softer' than DR, a 10% cross-field inconsistency rate is concerning. The claim of 'near-complete type-valid IE' is undermined when 1 in 10 entities has inconsistent typing.\\\" R1 给 major weakness，要求更强的 CF mitigation（不仅是 limitation 声明）。 R-F1=8.36% (+0.13pp, p=0.58) 在 median 档下被接受为 F1-neutral。\\n\"\n185\t  },\n186\t  {\n187\t    \"name\": \"SciERC full S2 (ablation)\",\n188\t    \"description\": \"Two-pass strategy: Pass 1 entity extraction (grammar-only)，Pass 2 relation generation (input-dependent grammar from Pass 1 entities)。\\n\",\n189\t    \"results\": {\n190\t      \"total_triples\": 1644,\n191\t      \"total_entities\": 2228,\n192\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n193\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n194\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0097,\n195\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0803,\n196\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.319,\n197\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0803\n198\t    },\n199\t    \"tables\": [\n200\t      \"Table 3 row 5 (or Appendix): S2 ablation metrics.\"\n201\t    ],\n202\t    \"figures\": [],\n203\t    \"analysis\": \"S2 数据在 median 档无争议——被接受为 ablation 即可。不要试图将 S2 包装为 CF 解决方案，审稿人会立刻拆穿。\\n\\n\\nS2 DR=0.97% ≈ S1 0.93%，CF=8.03% vs S1 9.90%（Δ-1.87pp，non-significant）。 Triples 减少（1644 vs 1729, -4.9%），F1 略低。Median 档下审稿人对 S2 反应冷淡： R2 写 \\\"S2 adds implementation complexity without clear benefit — DR comparable, CF marginally lower but not significantly so, and F1 drops. The authors correctly position this as an ablation rather than a contribution.\\\" R3 认为 S2 展示了 framework flexibility，acceptable as appendix material。 关键：S2 不解决 CF 的事实在 median 档下被 R1 引用为 \\\"even the two-pass variant cannot address CF, confirming this is a fundamental limitation of per-relation enforcement.\\\"\\n\"\n204\t  },\n205\t  {\n206\t    \"name\": \"DocRED unconstrained baseline\",\n207\t    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B DocRED unconstrained baseline (Phase 2 checker v2)。\\n\",\n208\t    \"results\": {\n209\t      \"documents_checked\": 986,\n210\t      \"parse_failures\": 12,\n211\t      \"total_entities\": 20171,\n212\t      \"total_triples\": 17497,\n213\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0248,\n214\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.2966,\n215\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1846,\n216\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n217\t      \"entity_f1\": 58.15,\n218\t      \"relation_f1\": 7.74\n219\t    },\n220\t    \"tables\": [\n221\t      \"Table 5 row 1: DocRED unconstrained baseline.\"\n222\t    ],\n223\t    \"figures\": [],\n224\t    \"analysis\": \"RV=29.66% baseline 是理解后续 grammar 层 F1 提升的关键。 Grammar 消除 OOV → all_set 方法下 fewer FP → higher precision。\\n\\n\\nRV=29.66% 是 DocRED 特有现象——96 relations 中很多 Qwen 生成的 relation names 不在 vocabulary 中。Median R2 会注意：\\\"Nearly 30% out-of-vocabulary rate suggests the model fundamentally struggles with this ontology's relation set, which confounds all downstream violation metrics.\\\" 这设置了 D014 dual-factor 叙事的伏笔。 E-F1=58.15% vs R-F1=7.74% 的巨大落差在 median 档被接受为 \\\"relation extraction is much harder than entity recognition in zero-shot setting.\\\"\\n\"\n225\t  },\n226\t  {\n227\t    \"name\": \"DocRED grammar-only\",\n228\t    \"description\": \"DocRED grammar-only，验证 grammar 层在高 RV 数据集上的独立效果。\\n\",\n229\t    \"results\": {\n230\t      \"documents_checked\": 985,\n231\t      \"parse_failures\": 13,\n232\t      \"total_entities\": 20150,\n233\t      \"total_triples\": 17341,\n234\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n235\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n236\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.2617,\n237\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0007,\n238\t      \"entity_f1\": 59.38,\n239\t      \"relation_f1\": 8.31\n240\t    },\n241\t    \"tables\": [\n242\t      \"Table 5 row 2: DocRED grammar-only.\"\n243\t    ],\n244\t    \"figures\": [],\n245\t    \"analysis\": \"Grammar-only DocRED 的 DR↑ 现象在 median 档是一个 moderate risk point。 R2 的 \\\"direct evidence\\\" 要求可通过 rebuttal 补充 triple-level tracing （抽样 100 个 grammar-corrected triples 追踪 before/after），effort ~2 天。\\n\\n\\n关键发现：grammar 消除 RV (29.66%→0.03%) 和 ET (2.48%→0%) 后，DR 反而上升 (18.46%→26.17%, +7.71pp)。这不是方法失败——grammar 将 OOV relation names 强制映射到 valid names，暴露了这些 triples 的 latent DR violations。 Median R2 会质疑：\\\"DR *increases* with grammar constraints? This seems to contradict the paper's narrative.\\\" 但 dual-factor 解释（grammar 揭露 latent violations）可部分说服。R2 给 major weakness 但标注 \\\"the dual-factor explanation is plausible but would benefit from direct evidence (e.g., tracing specific triples before/after grammar correction to verify the latent violation hypothesis).\\\" E-F1=59.38% 显著高于 unconstrained 58.15% (+1.23pp)——grammar 是 E-F1 唯一来源。\\n\"\n246\t  },\n247\t  {\n248\t    \"name\": \"DocRED semantic-only\",\n249\t    \"description\": \"DocRED semantic-only，验证无 grammar 保底时 semantic 层在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\\n\",\n250\t    \"results\": {\n251\t      \"documents_checked\": 987,\n252\t      \"parse_failures\": 11,\n253\t      \"total_entities\": 20185,\n254\t      \"total_triples\": 17571,\n255\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0422,\n256\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.2987,\n257\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1384,\n258\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0105,\n259\t      \"entity_f1\": 57.81,\n260\t      \"relation_f1\": 7.7\n261\t    },\n262\t    \"tables\": [\n263\t      \"Table 5 row 3: DocRED semantic-only.\"\n264\t    ],\n265\t    \"figures\": [],\n266\t    \"analysis\": \"Semantic-only 一致性（SciERC/DocRED 都是 ~24% DR reduction）支撑了 enabling dependency 叙事的 generalizability。\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only DR↓25%（18.46%→13.84%），与 SciERC semantic-only ↓24% 一致。 RV 基本不变（29.87%），ET 反而上升（2.48%→4.22%）——semantic 层在 OOV context 下可能干扰 entity type 生成。Median 档下此数据被视为 \\\"expected given the enabling dependency\\\" 叙事。R1 引用为 ablation 证据，无额外 concern。 E-F1=57.81% 低于 unconstrained 58.15%——semantic-only 对 DocRED 有轻微负效果， 但差异小且无显著性，不构成 concern。\\n\"\n267\t  },\n268\t  {\n269\t    \"name\": \"DocRED full S1\",\n270\t    \"description\": \"DocRED grammar+semantic S1，论文在 DocRED 上的主推配置。\\n\",\n271\t    \"results\": {\n272\t      \"documents_checked\": 987,\n273\t      \"parse_failures\": 11,\n274\t      \"total_entities\": 20187,\n275\t      \"total_triples\": 17341,\n276\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n277\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n278\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1021,\n279\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0257,\n280\t      \"entity_f1\": 59.37,\n281\t      \"relation_f1\": 8.23\n282\t    },\n283\t    \"tables\": [\n284\t      \"Table 5 row 4: DocRED full S1.\",\n285\t      \"Table 6: Constraint Coverage metric — SciERC vs DocRED fallback rates.\"\n286\t    ],\n287\t    \"figures\": [],\n288\t    \"analysis\": \"DocRED DR↓44.7% 在 median 档收到 1 个 major weakness。Rebuttal 策略： (a) 引入 Constraint Coverage metric 量化 semantic 层实际生效比例； (b) 强调 Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% 证明方法本身有效，Qwen 的弱表现是 model-specific； (c) 承认 \\\"for models with high OOV rates, the semantic layer's effective coverage is reduced\\\" 作为 honest limitation。Effort ~3 天。\\n\\n\\nDR↓44.7%（18.46%→10.21%）是 median 档的核心争议点。vs SciERC ↓94%，差距巨大。 R2 写 major weakness：\\\"The method achieves only 45% DR reduction on DocRED vs. 94% on SciERC. The authors' explanation ('tightness × RV baseline interaction') is partially convincing but raises the question: for real-world complex ontologies where RV is high, is the method practically useful?\\\"\\nDual-factor 解释（Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 揭露 latent DR → 残余 DR 更高）被 R2 评为 \\\"plausible but needs stronger evidence.\\\" R1 认为 Constraint Coverage 指标（SciERC ~89% vs DocRED ~43%）如果引入会 将此从 weakness 转为 quantifiable finding。R3 接受 dual-factor 解释。\\nR-F1=8.23% (+0.50pp, p<0.001) 和 E-F1=59.37% (+1.22pp, p<0.001) 的 显著提升被 3/3 审稿人承认。但 R2 补充 \\\"the F1 improvement is driven entirely by grammar eliminating OOV, not by the semantic constraint layer — this should be made more explicit.\\\"\\n\"\n289\t  },\n290\t  {\n291\t    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC unconstrained\",\n292\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B SciERC unconstrained，cross-model baseline。\\n\",\n293\t    \"results\": {\n294\t      \"total_entities\": 2451,\n295\t      \"total_relations\": 1274,\n296\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n297\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0055,\n298\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1334,\n299\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0024,\n300\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.2356,\n301\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0268,\n302\t      \"json_parse_failures\": 1\n303\t    },\n304\t    \"tables\": [\n305\t      \"Table 7 row 1: Llama SciERC unconstrained.\"\n306\t    ],\n307\t    \"figures\": [],\n308\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama 更低的 F1 在 median 档被视为 zero-shot variability，不威胁 constraint claim。\\n\\n\\nLlama SciERC DR=13.34% 略低于 Qwen 15.37%，RV=0.55% 也低——Llama 对 SciERC 7 个 relation names 掌握更好。但 R-F1=2.68% 远低于 Qwen 8.23%——Llama 在 此 prompt format 下 extraction quality 更差。 Median 档下 R3 注意到 \\\"Llama achieves much lower F1 than Qwen on the same task, suggesting the constraint evaluation may be confounded by model capability differences.\\\" 建议增加 few-shot 或 supervised 设置以 disentangle constraint effect from model capability。这是 minor suggestion，不构成 major weakness。\\n\"\n309\t  },\n310\t  {\n311\t    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC full S1\",\n312\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B SciERC full S1，cross-model constraint validation。\\n\",\n313\t    \"results\": {\n314\t      \"samples\": 550,\n315\t      \"entities_extracted\": 2469,\n316\t      \"relations_extracted\": 1315,\n317\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n318\t      \"relation_vocab_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n319\t      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n320\t      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0656,\n321\t      \"entity_f1\": 0.2349,\n322\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.0254\n323\t    },\n324\t    \"tables\": [\n325\t      \"Table 7 row 2: Llama SciERC full S1.\"\n326\t    ],\n327\t    \"figures\": [],\n328\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama SciERC 是 cross-model 叙事的基石。DR↓99.4% 远超 Qwen 的 ↓94%， 暗示 Llama 的低 RV baseline 允许 semantic 层更充分 enforce constraints。 这恰好支撑 D014 dual-factor insight。\\n\\n\\nDR=0.08% (↓99.4%)——比 Qwen 的 0.93% 还低，near-perfect constraint enforcement。 这是论文最强的 cross-model 证据。Median 档下 3/3 审稿人认可。 但 CF=6.56% 和 E-F1 下降（23.56%→23.49%, -0.07pp）被 R1 记录。 R-F1 下降（2.68%→2.54%, -0.14pp）被接受为 F1-neutral。 R3 写 \\\"Cross-model results on SciERC are strong — near-zero DR with no code modification. However, two models is the minimum for a generalization claim; the authors should clearly frame this as preliminary cross-model evidence.\\\"\\n\"\n329\t  },\n330\t  {\n331\t    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED unconstrained\",\n332\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B DocRED unconstrained，cross-model DocRED baseline。\\n\",\n333\t    \"results\": {\n334\t      \"documents\": 998,\n335\t      \"documents_checked\": 930,\n336\t      \"parse_failures\": 68,\n337\t      \"unique_entities\": 11525,\n338\t      \"total_triples\": 16437,\n339\t      \"ET_rate_pct\": 0.13,\n340\t      \"RV_rate_pct\": 16.03,\n341\t      \"DR_rate_pct\": 26.07,\n342\t      \"CF_rate_pct\": 0.17,\n343\t      \"entity_f1\": 55.65,\n344\t      \"relation_f1\": 5.98\n345\t    },\n346\t    \"tables\": [\n347\t      \"Table 7 row 3: Llama DocRED unconstrained.\"\n348\t    ],\n349\t    \"figures\": [],\n350\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama 高 parse failure 在 median 档被标为 limitation 而非 fatal flaw。 建议在 §5 正文（而非 footnote）讨论 parse failures 的影响。\\n\\n\\nLlama DocRED DR=26.07% 高于 Qwen 18.46%，但 RV=16.03% 远低于 Qwen 29.66%。 这是 D014 dual-factor 的直接证据：同一 ontology (τ̄=0.842) 下两个模型 DR 和 RV 呈反向关系。Parse failures=68/998 (6.8%) 远高于 Qwen 12/998 (1.2%)。 Median R2 写：\\\"Parse failure rate 5.6× higher for Llama is concerning. While the authors note this biases conservatively (failed parses excluded from F1), it suggests the model struggles with the output format.\\\" R3 建议 \\\"report parse failure rates prominently and discuss what output format issues cause them.\\\" Minor weakness。\\n\"\n351\t  },\n352\t  {\n353\t    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED full S1\",\n354\t    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B DocRED full S1，cross-model constraint 在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\\n\",\n355\t    \"results\": {\n356\t      \"documents\": 998,\n357\t      \"documents_checked\": 907,\n358\t      \"parse_failures\": 91,\n359\t      \"unique_entities\": 11296,\n360\t      \"triples\": 16368,\n361\t      \"ET\": 0.0,\n362\t      \"RV\": 0.0,\n363\t      \"DR\": 2.55,\n364\t      \"CF\": 12.02,\n365\t      \"entity_f1\": 55.01,\n366\t      \"relation_f1\": 6.27\n367\t    },\n368\t    \"tables\": [\n369\t      \"Table 7 row 4: Llama DocRED full S1.\",\n370\t      \"Table 8: Cross-model × cross-dataset DR reduction matrix (2×2).\"\n371\t    ],\n372\t    \"figures\": [],\n373\t    \"analysis\": \"Llama DocRED 在 median 档贡献两个 major findings 和一个 concern： (1) DR↓90.2% 证明方法有效（positive）； (2) Qwen vs Llama 差异验证 dual-factor（positive）； (3) CF=12.02% + E-F1↓ 加重 CF limitation severity。 Net effect: 审稿人认为 cross-model 数据 strengthens the paper overall 但 requires honest limitation discussion。\\n\\n\\nDR↓90.2%（26.07%→2.55%）远优于 Qwen DocRED ↓44.7%。这直接验证 D014 dual-factor： Llama RV baseline 低（16% vs 30%）→ grammar 层揭露的 latent DR violations 更少 → semantic 层有效覆盖更高 → DR reduction 更大。\\n但 CF=12.02% 是全矩阵最高值。R1 写 major weakness：\\\"CF reaches 12% on Llama DocRED — worse than Qwen's 9.9% on SciERC. The trend suggests CF scales with constraint complexity, raising concerns about applicability to real-world ontologies.\\\" 这加重了 CF concern 的 severity。\\nE-F1=55.01% vs unconstrained 55.65% (Δ-0.64pp)——Llama DocRED 是唯一出现 E-F1 下降的配置。Median R2 写：\\\"Entity F1 *decreases* for Llama on DocRED, contradicting the DocRED E-F1 improvement seen with Qwen. The cross-model effect is inconsistent.\\\" 但 Δ 较小且 R-F1 上升 (+0.29pp)，R2 给 minor weakness。\\nParse failures 从 68 增加到 91 (+33.8%)，constrained decoding 加重了 Llama 的 parse 问题。R3 注意到但不视为 major issue。\\n\"\n374\t  },\n375\t  {\n376\t    \"name\": \"S2 pilot (50 docs)\",\n377\t    \"description\": \"S2 strategy pilot on 50 SciERC docs，用于 early feasibility check。\\n\",\n378\t    \"results\": {\n379\t      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0205,\n380\t      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n381\t      \"relation_f1\": 0.1008,\n382\t      \"samples\": 50,\n383\t      \"predicted_relations\": 146\n384\t    },\n385\t    \"tables\": [],\n386\t    \"figures\": [],\n387\t    \"analysis\": \"Pilot 仅用于方法开发阶段的 sanity check。论文中不出现。\\n\\n\\nPilot DR=2.05% 在小样本下看起来不错，但 full run (P008) DR=0.97% 表明 pilot 高估了 DR（小样本方差）。Median 档下审稿人不会单独评价 pilot——已被 full run 取代。 论文中不应引用 pilot 数据（per paper_framing 指导：\\\"Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence\\\"）。\\n\"\n388\t  },\n389\t  {\n390\t    \"name\": \"Post-hoc filtering baseline\",\n391\t    \"description\": \"对 unconstrained output 执行 post-hoc filtering（删除所有 DR/RV/ET violating triples）， 作为 OntoCoDec 的 alternative baseline。\\n\",\n392\t    \"results\": {\n393\t      \"docred_f1_after\": 9.61,\n394\t      \"docred_precision_after\": 11.22,\n395\t      \"docred_recall_after\": 8.4,\n396\t      \"docred_rejection_rate\": 0.481,\n397\t      \"docred_tp_before\": 1137,\n398\t      \"docred_tp_after\": 1010,\n399\t      \"docred_tp_lost\": 127,\n400\t      \"docred_et_residual\": 0.0247,\n401\t      \"scierc_f1_after\": 8.63,\n402\t      \"scierc_rejection_rate\": 0.168,\n403\t      \"scierc_recall_after\": 10.68\n404\t    },\n405\t    \"tables\": [\n406\t      \"Table 9: OntoCoDec vs. post-hoc filtering — multi-dimensional comparison (F1, recall, rejection rate, ET residual, operational properties).\"\n407\t    ],\n408\t    \"figures\": [],\n409\t    \"analysis\": \"Post-hoc baseline 在 median 档被 R2 用来 challenge \\\"why constrained decoding?\\\" 叙事，但 multi-dimensional framing + 48.1% rejection rate + 127 TP loss 足以维持论文叙事。关键是不要 claim \\\"OntoCoDec is strictly better\\\" —— 诚实承认 precision/recall trade-off。\\n\\n\\nPost-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36; DocRED 9.61 vs 8.23）—— 这是 median 档 R2 的潜在 attack line：\\\"Why not just use post-hoc filtering? It achieves higher F1 AND zero violations.\\\"\\n但 multi-dimensional defense 在 median 档部分有效： - DocRED 丢弃 48.1% triples（R1 认为 \\\"unacceptable information loss\\\"） - 127 个 TP 被误删（11.2% of TPs） - Recall 下降（SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp）vs OntoCoDec recall 上升 - ET residual=2.47%（post-hoc 不能修 entity type）\\nR2 写 minor weakness：\\\"The comparison with post-hoc filtering needs clearer framing. In scenarios where precision matters more than recall, post-hoc may be preferred. The authors should acknowledge this explicitly rather than implying OntoCoDec is always superior.\\\" R1 接受 multi-dimensional framing，认为 operational advantages（流式、 无需后处理）有实际价值。\\n\"\n410\t  },\n411\t  {\n412\t    \"name\": \"Bootstrap CI (10000 iterations)\",\n413\t    \"description\": \"Document-level bootstrap (10000 resample) 计算 F1 差异的 confidence intervals 和 p-values。\\n\",\n414\t    \"results\": {\n415\t      \"scierc_rel_f1_delta\": 0.13,\n416\t      \"scierc_rel_f1_p\": 0.58,\n417\t      \"scierc_ent_f1_delta\": -0.03,\n418\t      \"scierc_ent_f1_p\": 0.53,\n419\t      \"docred_rel_f1_delta\": 0.5,\n420\t      \"docred_rel_f1_p\": \"<0.001\",\n421\t      \"docred_rel_f1_ci\": \"[+0.23, +0.81]\",\n422\t      \"docred_ent_f1_delta\": 1.23,\n423\t      \"docred_ent_f1_p\": \"<0.001\",\n424\t      \"docred_ent_f1_ci\": \"[+0.94, +1.55]\"\n425\t    },\n426\t    \"tables\": [\n427\t      \"Table 10: Bootstrap CI results for all metric pairs.\"\n428\t    ],\n429\t    \"figures\": [],\n430\t    \"analysis\": \"Bootstrap 数据在 median 档被全部接受为 methodologically sound。 争议点不在统计方法而在 interpretation——R2 要求更清晰的 mechanism attribution， R1 要求 F1 regime sensitivity discussion。两者都是 rebuttal 可回应的。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI 提供了严格的统计证据。Median 档下： - SciERC F1-neutral (p=0.58/0.53) 被 3/3 审稿人接受——constraint 不降 F1。 - DocRED F1 显著提升 (p<0.001) 被承认但 R2 追问 mechanism。\\nR2 写：\\\"The significant F1 improvement on DocRED is driven by grammar eliminating OOV predictions (which count as FP under all_set), not by the semantic layer improving extraction. The authors should clarify that this is an artifact of the evaluation methodology (all_set) interacting with grammar constraints, not a genuine improvement in extraction capability.\\\" 这是 fair point——论文需明确归因（grammar→OOV elimination→fewer FP→higher precision）。\\nR1 建议 \\\"In the zero-shot low-F1 regime, even small absolute gains are percentage-wise significant. Discuss whether these gains would persist at higher F1 levels.\\\" 这引出 F1 regime sensitivity discussion。\\n\"\n431\t  },\n432\t  {\n433\t    \"name\": \"DocRED schema compilation (Phase 0 R2)\",\n434\t    \"description\": \"DocRED Phase 0 重跑（被 kill，已被 P004 取代）。\\n\",\n435\t    \"results\": {\n436\t      \"status\": \"killed\",\n437\t      \"superseded_by\": \"P004\"\n438\t    },\n439\t    \"tables\": [],\n440\t    \"figures\": [],\n441\t    \"analysis\": \"N/A — killed experiment, no paper impact.\\n\\n实验被终止，不进入论文。Median 档审稿人不会看到此实验。\\n\"\n442\t  }\n443\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dfc5dc4-a95d-4cb7-b790-c6ab597d3a86","uuid":"8486199f-b714-42eb-9513-c45bffd7501d","timestamp":"2026-05-14T21:14:02.139Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260514T205155/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B zero-shot SciERC extraction，minimal prompt，测量 baseline violation rates。 7 relations, 551 abstracts。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 1724,\n      \"total_entities\": 2474,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 1.0,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0139,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1537,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.3101,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0823,\n      \"per_relation_dr_top3\": {\n        \"Compare\": 0.4242,\n        \"Feature-of\": 0.3354,\n        \"Part-of\": 0.25\n      },\n      \"per_relation_dr_bottom2\": {\n        \"Used-for\": 0.0076,\n        \"Conjunction\": 0.0\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1: Per-relation DR violation rates (SciERC, minimal prompt). 7 relations ranked by tightness τ.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"R2 在 median 档会写：\\\"The violation landscape analysis (§3) provides useful empirical grounding, but the causal claim that 'violation rate is driven by tightness' is overstated given confounds (relation frequency, entity type distribution).\\\" 需在 rebuttal 中降级为 correlational + 补充 frequency 作为 covariate 的分析。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档下，15.4% DR baseline 被 2/3 审稿人接受为 non-trivial。R2 可能质疑： \\\"zero-shot 本身就会产生各种错误，15% constraint violation 在 8% F1 下是否真的重要？\\\" 但 per-relation 分布（Compare 42%、Used-for 0.8%）的极端差异足以说服—— 这不是随机错误，是 constraint tightness 相关的系统性现象。 R1 接受此数据作为 motivation。R3 认为 violation landscape 是独立贡献。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B SciERC，schema-informed prompt 将 domain/range constraints 写入 prompt， 测量 prompt-level intervention 效果。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0578,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.003,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"total_triples\": 1661,\n      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct\": -62.4,\n      \"per_relation_notable\": {\n        \"Feature-of_delta_pp\": -22.3,\n        \"Part-of_delta_pp\": -22.5,\n        \"Compare_delta_pp\": -14.8,\n        \"Evaluate-for_delta_pp\": 5.8\n      },\n      \"mcnemar_significant\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2: Per-relation DR rates under minimal vs. schema-informed prompts, with McNemar test results.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Schema-informed prompt 数据在 median 档基本无争议，支撑 Claim 2。 Evaluate-for 回归是一个 talking point 但不构成 major weakness。\\n\\n\\n62.4% reduction 在 median 档被全部审稿人接受为 \\\"substantial but insufficient\\\"。 关键攻击面是 Evaluate-for 回归 (+5.8pp)：R2 会写 \\\"The fact that prompting can *increase* violations for specific relation types (Evaluate-for, §3.2) is an interesting finding but needs more analysis — is this a prior-constraint conflict or simply noise?\\\" Median 档下 R2 对此提出 minor weakness 而非 major，因为论文已有 prior-constraint conflict 解释框架。但 R2 建议 \\\"run significance test on per-relation changes to distinguish real regression from variance.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (minimal prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B DocRED (998 docs, 96 relations)，minimal prompt baseline。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_docs\": 998,\n      \"parsed_docs\": 962,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.964,\n      \"total_entities\": 19099,\n      \"total_triples\": 16540,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.075,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.289,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.187,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n      \"top_dr_by_rate\": {\n        \"P35_head_of_state\": 1.0,\n        \"P710_participant\": 0.919,\n        \"P172_ethnic_group\": 0.875\n      },\n      \"top_dr_by_count\": {\n        \"P31_instance_of\": {\n          \"violations\": 322,\n          \"total\": 533,\n          \"rate\": 0.604\n        },\n        \"P1001_applies_to_jurisdiction\": {\n          \"violations\": 264,\n          \"total\": 594,\n          \"rate\": 0.444\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 1 (extended): DocRED violation rates. Top-10 relations by DR rate and count.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RV=28.9% 是 DocRED 特有现象（96 relations 中很多 Qwen 未见过）。 Median R2 会追问 \\\"如果先修 RV 再测 DR，DR 会不会更低？\\\"——恰好引出 grammar_only 实验。\\n\\n\\nDocRED 18.7% DR vs SciERC 15.4%——14× ontology size 差异下 violation rate 相近—— 直接支撑 \\\"violation rate driven by tightness not ontology size\\\" claim。 Median 档下 R1 接受此 finding。R2 会注意到 RV=28.9% 极高，质疑： \\\"Nearly 30% of generated relation names are out-of-vocabulary — how much of DR is confounded by the model simply not knowing the relation names?\\\" 这是 D014 dual-factor insight 的前兆。R2 不会因此 reject 但会要求 disentangle RV 和 DR 的交互效应。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED violation rate (schema-informed prompt)\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED schema-informed prompt，测量 prompt-level 在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_documents\": 998,\n      \"documents_checked\": 943,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 0.9449,\n      \"total_triples\": 16782,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0061,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.1841,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1284,\n      \"vs_minimal_dr_reduction_pct\": -31.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 2 (DocRED section): Schema-informed prompt results.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Prompt insufficiency claim (C2) 在 median 档获得 3/3 审稿人支持。 这是论文最安全的 claim——数据清晰，叙事直觉合理。\\n\\n\\nDR↓31.3% vs SciERC ↓62.4%——prompt intervention 在复杂 ontology 上效果减半。 Median 档下所有审稿人接受此数据。R2 会标注 \\\"The scaling gap between SciERC (62%) and DocRED (31%) prompt-level reduction is compelling evidence for Claim 2, though confounded by the 96-relation prompt being much longer and potentially overwhelming the model's attention.\\\" 这是 minor point，不构成 major weakness。 R1 认为此数据强化了 decoding-time 方法的 motivation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"Phase 2 SciERC unconstrained（与 Phase 0 同 pipeline 但 Phase 2 checker v2）， 作为 ablation 的 control condition。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_samples\": 551,\n      \"total_triples\": 1724,\n      \"total_entities\": 2474,\n      \"json_parse_rate\": 1.0,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0139,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1537,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.3101,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0823\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3 row 1: SciERC unconstrained baseline metrics.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Baseline 数据确保 ablation 有公平比较基准。F1=8.23% 的 low absolute value 在 median 档下被 R2 提及一次（\\\"results are in very low F1 regime\\\"）但被 zero-shot framing 部分化解（R3 接受，R2 remains skeptical）。\\n\\n\\n与 P001 数值一致（同模型同数据同 prompt，仅 checker 版本更新后数值不变）。 Median 档下此实验本身无争议，仅作为 ablation table 的 row 0。 R2 可能注意到 R-F1=8.23% 绝对值低，引出 C8 concern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC grammar-only\",\n    \"description\": \"仅启用 grammar layer (XGrammar CFG)，验证 grammar 层对 violation 的独立效果。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 1725,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1484,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.3098,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0823\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3 row 2: SciERC grammar-only.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Grammar-only 是 enabling dependency 叙事的关键证据。DR 不降说明 grammar 是 semantic 的 prerequisite 而非 replacement。\\n\\n\\nGrammar 层消除 ET/RV（→0%）但 DR 几乎不变（15.37%→14.84%，Δ-0.53pp）—— 完美演示 grammar 只管 vocabulary 不管 semantics。Median 档下 3/3 审稿人认为 此 ablation 清晰有效。R1 可能评价 \\\"The ablation clearly demonstrates the orthogonal contributions of the two layers — grammar handles vocabulary, semantic handles domain/range.\\\" CF=0.08% 也证明 grammar 层不引入 CF——CF 100% 来自 semantic 层。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC semantic-only\",\n    \"description\": \"仅启用 semantic layer (TypeConstraintProcessor)，无 grammar 保底。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 1726,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.004,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0151,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1165,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0271,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.3101,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0815\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3 row 3: SciERC semantic-only.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semantic-only 的 CF=2.71% 已开始上升（unconstrained 0.08%），预示 semantic enforcement 的 CF 副作用。完整 ablation 梯度：unconstrained 0.08% → semantic_only 2.71% → full_s1 9.90%。R1 会注意到此趋势。\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only DR↓24%（vs full_s1 ↓94%）——没有 grammar 保底时 semantic 层遇到 OOV relation types 无法 enforce constraints，效果大打折扣。RV=1.51% 残余证明 semantic 不管 vocabulary。Median 档下此数据被 R1 引用为 \\\"convincing evidence for the enabling dependency between layers.\\\" R2 同意但追问 \\\"What fraction of the 76% gap (24% vs 94%) is due to OOV vs. other failure modes?\\\" 需 rebuttal 补充 OOV relation 占 semantic failure 的比例分析。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"Grammar + Semantic 双层，single-pass (S1)。论文主推配置。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 1729,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0093,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.099,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.3098,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0836\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3 row 4: SciERC full S1 — primary configuration.\",\n      \"Table 4: DR reduction per relation type (unconstrained → S1).\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median R1 的 CF major concern 是可回应的：提供 CF 子类型分析（EVR 占 >90%， 根因是 type system 语义模糊），补充 ablation 证明 CF 100% 由 semantic 层引入， 并提出 future work direction（global entity-type consensus）。但需要 rebuttal 中 实际补充这些分析，不能仅靠声明。估计 rebuttal effort 3-4 天。\\n\\n\\nDR=0.93% (↓94%) 是论文最强数据点。Median 档下 R1 和 R3 对 DR 结果高度满意。 但 CF=9.90% 是 #1 攻击面：R1 写 \\\"The method trades DR violations (15.4%→0.93%) for CF violations (0.08%→9.90%). While the authors argue CF is 'softer' than DR, a 10% cross-field inconsistency rate is concerning. The claim of 'near-complete type-valid IE' is undermined when 1 in 10 entities has inconsistent typing.\\\" R1 给 major weakness，要求更强的 CF mitigation（不仅是 limitation 声明）。 R-F1=8.36% (+0.13pp, p=0.58) 在 median 档下被接受为 F1-neutral。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SciERC full S2 (ablation)\",\n    \"description\": \"Two-pass strategy: Pass 1 entity extraction (grammar-only)，Pass 2 relation generation (input-dependent grammar from Pass 1 entities)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_triples\": 1644,\n      \"total_entities\": 2228,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0097,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0803,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.319,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0803\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 3 row 5 (or Appendix): S2 ablation metrics.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"S2 数据在 median 档无争议——被接受为 ablation 即可。不要试图将 S2 包装为 CF 解决方案，审稿人会立刻拆穿。\\n\\n\\nS2 DR=0.97% ≈ S1 0.93%，CF=8.03% vs S1 9.90%（Δ-1.87pp，non-significant）。 Triples 减少（1644 vs 1729, -4.9%），F1 略低。Median 档下审稿人对 S2 反应冷淡： R2 写 \\\"S2 adds implementation complexity without clear benefit — DR comparable, CF marginally lower but not significantly so, and F1 drops. The authors correctly position this as an ablation rather than a contribution.\\\" R3 认为 S2 展示了 framework flexibility，acceptable as appendix material。 关键：S2 不解决 CF 的事实在 median 档下被 R1 引用为 \\\"even the two-pass variant cannot address CF, confirming this is a fundamental limitation of per-relation enforcement.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED unconstrained baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen3-8B DocRED unconstrained baseline (Phase 2 checker v2)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents_checked\": 986,\n      \"parse_failures\": 12,\n      \"total_entities\": 20171,\n      \"total_triples\": 17497,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0248,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.2966,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1846,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.001,\n      \"entity_f1\": 58.15,\n      \"relation_f1\": 7.74\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5 row 1: DocRED unconstrained baseline.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RV=29.66% baseline 是理解后续 grammar 层 F1 提升的关键。 Grammar 消除 OOV → all_set 方法下 fewer FP → higher precision。\\n\\n\\nRV=29.66% 是 DocRED 特有现象——96 relations 中很多 Qwen 生成的 relation names 不在 vocabulary 中。Median R2 会注意：\\\"Nearly 30% out-of-vocabulary rate suggests the model fundamentally struggles with this ontology's relation set, which confounds all downstream violation metrics.\\\" 这设置了 D014 dual-factor 叙事的伏笔。 E-F1=58.15% vs R-F1=7.74% 的巨大落差在 median 档被接受为 \\\"relation extraction is much harder than entity recognition in zero-shot setting.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED grammar-only\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED grammar-only，验证 grammar 层在高 RV 数据集上的独立效果。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents_checked\": 985,\n      \"parse_failures\": 13,\n      \"total_entities\": 20150,\n      \"total_triples\": 17341,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.2617,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0007,\n      \"entity_f1\": 59.38,\n      \"relation_f1\": 8.31\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5 row 2: DocRED grammar-only.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Grammar-only DocRED 的 DR↑ 现象在 median 档是一个 moderate risk point。 R2 的 \\\"direct evidence\\\" 要求可通过 rebuttal 补充 triple-level tracing （抽样 100 个 grammar-corrected triples 追踪 before/after），effort ~2 天。\\n\\n\\n关键发现：grammar 消除 RV (29.66%→0.03%) 和 ET (2.48%→0%) 后，DR 反而上升 (18.46%→26.17%, +7.71pp)。这不是方法失败——grammar 将 OOV relation names 强制映射到 valid names，暴露了这些 triples 的 latent DR violations。 Median R2 会质疑：\\\"DR *increases* with grammar constraints? This seems to contradict the paper's narrative.\\\" 但 dual-factor 解释（grammar 揭露 latent violations）可部分说服。R2 给 major weakness 但标注 \\\"the dual-factor explanation is plausible but would benefit from direct evidence (e.g., tracing specific triples before/after grammar correction to verify the latent violation hypothesis).\\\" E-F1=59.38% 显著高于 unconstrained 58.15% (+1.23pp)——grammar 是 E-F1 唯一来源。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED semantic-only\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED semantic-only，验证无 grammar 保底时 semantic 层在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents_checked\": 987,\n      \"parse_failures\": 11,\n      \"total_entities\": 20185,\n      \"total_triples\": 17571,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0422,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.2987,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1384,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0105,\n      \"entity_f1\": 57.81,\n      \"relation_f1\": 7.7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5 row 3: DocRED semantic-only.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Semantic-only 一致性（SciERC/DocRED 都是 ~24% DR reduction）支撑了 enabling dependency 叙事的 generalizability。\\n\\n\\nSemantic-only DR↓25%（18.46%→13.84%），与 SciERC semantic-only ↓24% 一致。 RV 基本不变（29.87%），ET 反而上升（2.48%→4.22%）——semantic 层在 OOV context 下可能干扰 entity type 生成。Median 档下此数据被视为 \\\"expected given the enabling dependency\\\" 叙事。R1 引用为 ablation 证据，无额外 concern。 E-F1=57.81% 低于 unconstrained 58.15%——semantic-only 对 DocRED 有轻微负效果， 但差异小且无显著性，不构成 concern。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED grammar+semantic S1，论文在 DocRED 上的主推配置。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents_checked\": 987,\n      \"parse_failures\": 11,\n      \"total_entities\": 20187,\n      \"total_triples\": 17341,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0003,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1021,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0257,\n      \"entity_f1\": 59.37,\n      \"relation_f1\": 8.23\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 5 row 4: DocRED full S1.\",\n      \"Table 6: Constraint Coverage metric — SciERC vs DocRED fallback rates.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"DocRED DR↓44.7% 在 median 档收到 1 个 major weakness。Rebuttal 策略： (a) 引入 Constraint Coverage metric 量化 semantic 层实际生效比例； (b) 强调 Llama DocRED DR↓90.2% 证明方法本身有效，Qwen 的弱表现是 model-specific； (c) 承认 \\\"for models with high OOV rates, the semantic layer's effective coverage is reduced\\\" 作为 honest limitation。Effort ~3 天。\\n\\n\\nDR↓44.7%（18.46%→10.21%）是 median 档的核心争议点。vs SciERC ↓94%，差距巨大。 R2 写 major weakness：\\\"The method achieves only 45% DR reduction on DocRED vs. 94% on SciERC. The authors' explanation ('tightness × RV baseline interaction') is partially convincing but raises the question: for real-world complex ontologies where RV is high, is the method practically useful?\\\"\\nDual-factor 解释（Qwen RV=29.66% >> Llama RV=16.03% → grammar 揭露 latent DR → 残余 DR 更高）被 R2 评为 \\\"plausible but needs stronger evidence.\\\" R1 认为 Constraint Coverage 指标（SciERC ~89% vs DocRED ~43%）如果引入会 将此从 weakness 转为 quantifiable finding。R3 接受 dual-factor 解释。\\nR-F1=8.23% (+0.50pp, p<0.001) 和 E-F1=59.37% (+1.22pp, p<0.001) 的 显著提升被 3/3 审稿人承认。但 R2 补充 \\\"the F1 improvement is driven entirely by grammar eliminating OOV, not by the semantic constraint layer — this should be made more explicit.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC unconstrained\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B SciERC unconstrained，cross-model baseline。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_entities\": 2451,\n      \"total_relations\": 1274,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0055,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.1334,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0024,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.2356,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0268,\n      \"json_parse_failures\": 1\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 row 1: Llama SciERC unconstrained.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama 更低的 F1 在 median 档被视为 zero-shot variability，不威胁 constraint claim。\\n\\n\\nLlama SciERC DR=13.34% 略低于 Qwen 15.37%，RV=0.55% 也低——Llama 对 SciERC 7 个 relation names 掌握更好。但 R-F1=2.68% 远低于 Qwen 8.23%——Llama 在 此 prompt format 下 extraction quality 更差。 Median 档下 R3 注意到 \\\"Llama achieves much lower F1 than Qwen on the same task, suggesting the constraint evaluation may be confounded by model capability differences.\\\" 建议增加 few-shot 或 supervised 设置以 disentangle constraint effect from model capability。这是 minor suggestion，不构成 major weakness。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama SciERC full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B SciERC full S1，cross-model constraint validation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"samples\": 550,\n      \"entities_extracted\": 2469,\n      \"relations_extracted\": 1315,\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0008,\n      \"relation_vocab_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"entity_type_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"cross_field_consistency_violation_rate\": 0.0656,\n      \"entity_f1\": 0.2349,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.0254\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 row 2: Llama SciERC full S1.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama SciERC 是 cross-model 叙事的基石。DR↓99.4% 远超 Qwen 的 ↓94%， 暗示 Llama 的低 RV baseline 允许 semantic 层更充分 enforce constraints。 这恰好支撑 D014 dual-factor insight。\\n\\n\\nDR=0.08% (↓99.4%)——比 Qwen 的 0.93% 还低，near-perfect constraint enforcement。 这是论文最强的 cross-model 证据。Median 档下 3/3 审稿人认可。 但 CF=6.56% 和 E-F1 下降（23.56%→23.49%, -0.07pp）被 R1 记录。 R-F1 下降（2.68%→2.54%, -0.14pp）被接受为 F1-neutral。 R3 写 \\\"Cross-model results on SciERC are strong — near-zero DR with no code modification. However, two models is the minimum for a generalization claim; the authors should clearly frame this as preliminary cross-model evidence.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED unconstrained\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B DocRED unconstrained，cross-model DocRED baseline。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents\": 998,\n      \"documents_checked\": 930,\n      \"parse_failures\": 68,\n      \"unique_entities\": 11525,\n      \"total_triples\": 16437,\n      \"ET_rate_pct\": 0.13,\n      \"RV_rate_pct\": 16.03,\n      \"DR_rate_pct\": 26.07,\n      \"CF_rate_pct\": 0.17,\n      \"entity_f1\": 55.65,\n      \"relation_f1\": 5.98\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 row 3: Llama DocRED unconstrained.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama 高 parse failure 在 median 档被标为 limitation 而非 fatal flaw。 建议在 §5 正文（而非 footnote）讨论 parse failures 的影响。\\n\\n\\nLlama DocRED DR=26.07% 高于 Qwen 18.46%，但 RV=16.03% 远低于 Qwen 29.66%。 这是 D014 dual-factor 的直接证据：同一 ontology (τ̄=0.842) 下两个模型 DR 和 RV 呈反向关系。Parse failures=68/998 (6.8%) 远高于 Qwen 12/998 (1.2%)。 Median R2 写：\\\"Parse failure rate 5.6× higher for Llama is concerning. While the authors note this biases conservatively (failed parses excluded from F1), it suggests the model struggles with the output format.\\\" R3 建议 \\\"report parse failure rates prominently and discuss what output format issues cause them.\\\" Minor weakness。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Llama DocRED full S1\",\n    \"description\": \"Llama-3.1-8B DocRED full S1，cross-model constraint 在复杂 ontology 上的效果。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"documents\": 998,\n      \"documents_checked\": 907,\n      \"parse_failures\": 91,\n      \"unique_entities\": 11296,\n      \"triples\": 16368,\n      \"ET\": 0.0,\n      \"RV\": 0.0,\n      \"DR\": 2.55,\n      \"CF\": 12.02,\n      \"entity_f1\": 55.01,\n      \"relation_f1\": 6.27\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 7 row 4: Llama DocRED full S1.\",\n      \"Table 8: Cross-model × cross-dataset DR reduction matrix (2×2).\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Llama DocRED 在 median 档贡献两个 major findings 和一个 concern： (1) DR↓90.2% 证明方法有效（positive）； (2) Qwen vs Llama 差异验证 dual-factor（positive）； (3) CF=12.02% + E-F1↓ 加重 CF limitation severity。 Net effect: 审稿人认为 cross-model 数据 strengthens the paper overall 但 requires honest limitation discussion。\\n\\n\\nDR↓90.2%（26.07%→2.55%）远优于 Qwen DocRED ↓44.7%。这直接验证 D014 dual-factor： Llama RV baseline 低（16% vs 30%）→ grammar 层揭露的 latent DR violations 更少 → semantic 层有效覆盖更高 → DR reduction 更大。\\n但 CF=12.02% 是全矩阵最高值。R1 写 major weakness：\\\"CF reaches 12% on Llama DocRED — worse than Qwen's 9.9% on SciERC. The trend suggests CF scales with constraint complexity, raising concerns about applicability to real-world ontologies.\\\" 这加重了 CF concern 的 severity。\\nE-F1=55.01% vs unconstrained 55.65% (Δ-0.64pp)——Llama DocRED 是唯一出现 E-F1 下降的配置。Median R2 写：\\\"Entity F1 *decreases* for Llama on DocRED, contradicting the DocRED E-F1 improvement seen with Qwen. The cross-model effect is inconsistent.\\\" 但 Δ 较小且 R-F1 上升 (+0.29pp)，R2 给 minor weakness。\\nParse failures 从 68 增加到 91 (+33.8%)，constrained decoding 加重了 Llama 的 parse 问题。R3 注意到但不视为 major issue。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"S2 pilot (50 docs)\",\n    \"description\": \"S2 strategy pilot on 50 SciERC docs，用于 early feasibility check。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"domain_range_violation_rate\": 0.0205,\n      \"relation_vocabulary_violation_rate\": 0.0,\n      \"relation_f1\": 0.1008,\n      \"samples\": 50,\n      \"predicted_relations\": 146\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Pilot 仅用于方法开发阶段的 sanity check。论文中不出现。\\n\\n\\nPilot DR=2.05% 在小样本下看起来不错，但 full run (P008) DR=0.97% 表明 pilot 高估了 DR（小样本方差）。Median 档下审稿人不会单独评价 pilot——已被 full run 取代。 论文中不应引用 pilot 数据（per paper_framing 指导：\\\"Do NOT cite pilot50 DR=0% as S2 evidence\\\"）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Post-hoc filtering baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"对 unconstrained output 执行 post-hoc filtering（删除所有 DR/RV/ET violating triples）， 作为 OntoCoDec 的 alternative baseline。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"docred_f1_after\": 9.61,\n      \"docred_precision_after\": 11.22,\n      \"docred_recall_after\": 8.4,\n      \"docred_rejection_rate\": 0.481,\n      \"docred_tp_before\": 1137,\n      \"docred_tp_after\": 1010,\n      \"docred_tp_lost\": 127,\n      \"docred_et_residual\": 0.0247,\n      \"scierc_f1_after\": 8.63,\n      \"scierc_rejection_rate\": 0.168,\n      \"scierc_recall_after\": 10.68\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 9: OntoCoDec vs. post-hoc filtering — multi-dimensional comparison (F1, recall, rejection rate, ET residual, operational properties).\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Post-hoc baseline 在 median 档被 R2 用来 challenge \\\"why constrained decoding?\\\" 叙事，但 multi-dimensional framing + 48.1% rejection rate + 127 TP loss 足以维持论文叙事。关键是不要 claim \\\"OntoCoDec is strictly better\\\" —— 诚实承认 precision/recall trade-off。\\n\\n\\nPost-hoc F1 > OntoCoDec F1（SciERC 8.63 vs 8.36; DocRED 9.61 vs 8.23）—— 这是 median 档 R2 的潜在 attack line：\\\"Why not just use post-hoc filtering? It achieves higher F1 AND zero violations.\\\"\\n但 multi-dimensional defense 在 median 档部分有效： - DocRED 丢弃 48.1% triples（R1 认为 \\\"unacceptable information loss\\\"） - 127 个 TP 被误删（11.2% of TPs） - Recall 下降（SciERC -0.72pp, DocRED -1.06pp）vs OntoCoDec recall 上升 - ET residual=2.47%（post-hoc 不能修 entity type）\\nR2 写 minor weakness：\\\"The comparison with post-hoc filtering needs clearer framing. In scenarios where precision matters more than recall, post-hoc may be preferred. The authors should acknowledge this explicitly rather than implying OntoCoDec is always superior.\\\" R1 接受 multi-dimensional framing，认为 operational advantages（流式、 无需后处理）有实际价值。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Bootstrap CI (10000 iterations)\",\n    \"description\": \"Document-level bootstrap (10000 resample) 计算 F1 差异的 confidence intervals 和 p-values。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scierc_rel_f1_delta\": 0.13,\n      \"scierc_rel_f1_p\": 0.58,\n      \"scierc_ent_f1_delta\": -0.03,\n      \"scierc_ent_f1_p\": 0.53,\n      \"docred_rel_f1_delta\": 0.5,\n      \"docred_rel_f1_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"docred_rel_f1_ci\": \"[+0.23, +0.81]\",\n      \"docred_ent_f1_delta\": 1.23,\n      \"docred_ent_f1_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"docred_ent_f1_ci\": \"[+0.94, +1.55]\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      \"Table 10: Bootstrap CI results for all metric pairs.\"\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Bootstrap 数据在 median 档被全部接受为 methodologically sound。 争议点不在统计方法而在 interpretation——R2 要求更清晰的 mechanism attribution， R1 要求 F1 regime sensitivity discussion。两者都是 rebuttal 可回应的。\\n\\n\\nBootstrap CI 提供了严格的统计证据。Median 档下： - SciERC F1-neutral (p=0.58/0.53) 被 3/3 审稿人接受——constraint 不降 F1。 - DocRED F1 显著提升 (p<0.001) 被承认但 R2 追问 mechanism。\\nR2 写：\\\"The significant F1 improvement on DocRED is driven by grammar eliminating OOV predictions (which count as FP under all_set), not by the semantic layer improving extraction. The authors should clarify that this is an artifact of the evaluation methodology (all_set) interacting with grammar constraints, not a genuine improvement in extraction capability.\\\" 这是 fair point——论文需明确归因（grammar→OOV elimination→fewer FP→higher precision）。\\nR1 建议 \\\"In the zero-shot low-F1 regime, even small absolute gains are percentage-wise significant. Discuss whether these gains would persist at higher F1 levels.\\\" 这引出 F1 regime sensitivity discussion。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"DocRED schema compilation (Phase 0 R2)\",\n    \"description\": \"DocRED Phase 0 重跑（被 kill，已被 P004 取代）。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"killed\",\n      \"superseded_by\": \"P004\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"N/A — killed experiment, no paper impact.\\n\\n实验被终止，不进入论文。Median 档审稿人不会看到此实验。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":443,"startLine":1,"totalLines":443}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Y2QNJ9Ft5KhNTTMBgHptCj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me write the LaTeX paper. I need to:\n\n1. Follow the median tier narrative guidance:\n   - Title with qualifier 'under Single-Relation Scope'\n   - Claim 1 tightness insight downgraded from causal to correlational\n   - §5 add Constraint Coverage ablation, turning DocRED weak effect into 'predictable from coverage metric' positive finding\n   - Strengthen §3 violation landscape independent contribution + decidability taxonomy formalism\n   - Add F1 regime sensitivity discussion\n\n2. Cover ALL experiments in the data:\n   - SciERC and DocRED violation rates across minimal and schema-informed prompts\n   - SciERC ablation studies isolating grammar-only, semantic-only, and full constraint configurations\n   - DocRED unconstrained baseline for comparison\n   - Grammar-only, semantic-only, and full constraint results for DocRED\n   - Llama model results on both SciERC and DocRED with unconstrained and full constraint variants\n   - Post-hoc filtering baseline and bootstrap confidence intervals\n   - Skipping the S2 pilot and the killed DocRED schema compilation experiment\n\nThat leaves 18 experiments to report. Now I'm structuring the paper with an abstract, introduction covering the violation landscape study and decidability taxonomy, the OntoCoDec framework section, experiments with constraint coverage ablation, related work, and conclusion. I'll need tables showing per-relation violation rates across both datasets, comparisons between minimal and schema-informed prompts, and full ablations for both SciERC and DocRED.\n\nI'm also planning cross-model comparisons between Llama and Qwen, post-hoc filtering results, and bootstrap confidence intervals. Let me pull the specific numbers from the experiment data to populate these tables accurately—starting with the violation landscape showing domain relation rates around 15% for SciERC and 19% for DocRED, with per-relation breakdowns where Compare violations hit 42% while Conjunction stays at zero. Generating ablation tables... Generating markdown table...\n\nNow I'm looking at the bootstrap confidence intervals to assess statistical significance—the relation extraction metrics show meaningful improvements for DocRED with p-values well below 0.001, while SciERC doesn't reach significance. I'm thinking about how to format this as a proper conference paper, probably using the EMNLP template.\n\nFor the title, I need to balance clarity with the constraint about single-relation scope—something like \"OntoCoDec: Near-Complete Type-Valid Information Extraction under Single-Relation Scope via Compiled Ontology Constraints\" captures the key contribution without being too unwieldy.\n\nWriting the full paper now...\n\nSetting up the LaTeX document... Now I'm looking at the specific violation metrics for SciERC across both the minimal prompt and schema-informed approaches. The minimal setup shows substantial room for improvement, with domain relation violations at over 15% and notable per-relation variation—Compare relations are particularly problematic at 42%, while Conjunction violations are nearly absent. The schema-informed version cuts the domain relation violations down to under 6%, representing a significant 62% relative reduction, and the per-relation improvements are substantial across most categories, with McNemar's test confirming statistical significance.\n\nMoving to DocRED, I'm seeing a much larger dataset with nearly 17,000 triples across almost 1,000 documents. The domain relation violation rate sits at 18.7%, with certain relations like head_of_state and ethnic_group showing near-perfect violation rates while others like instance_of and applies_to_jurisdiction have more moderate violations. When applying the schema-informed approach, the domain relation violations drop to about 13%, a 31% relative improvement, though the reduction is less dramatic than what we saw with SciERC. Now I'm looking at the ablation results for DocRED, comparing unconstrained versus grammar-only and semantic-only approaches, where the unconstrained model shows notably higher recall variance and entity F1 scores. I'm also starting to examine cross-model performance with Llama on SciERC. Now I'm looking at the bootstrap confidence intervals for both datasets—SciERC shows no significant changes in either metric, but DocRED shows substantial improvements with high statistical significance. Let me verify the entity F1 score for S2 in Table 3, which appears to be around 31.9%.\n\nI'm noticing an inconsistency in how the F1 values are scaled across experiments: SciERC reports them as fractions (like 0.3101 for 31.01%), while DocRED uses percentages directly (58.15 means 58.15%), and the Llama SciERC results also use fractions. I need to be careful about this scaling difference when comparing across datasets.\n\nNow I'm cross-checking the DocRED baseline numbers—the Phase 2 unconstrained result (18.46%) is the right one to use as the baseline for the ablation table, while the Phase 0 minimal prompt result (18.7%) comes from a different checker version and is better suited for the violation landscape analysis.\n\nSciERC shows consistent numbers across both conditions at 15.37%, so there's no discrepancy there. With these clarifications sorted out, I'm ready to move forward with writing. For the constraint coverage ablation in section 5, I need to examine how the semantic layer's effective coverage varies between different setups.\n\nLooking at the fallback data, DocRED has substantially more fallbacks per document compared to SciERC—about 5.3 times higher—which translates to constraint coverage of roughly 89% for SciERC versus 43% for DocRED. I'll define constraint coverage as the proportion of constrained token positions where the semantic mask is actually active rather than falling back to grammar-only processing.\n\nNow I'm going to write out the full LaTeX document. I'll start composing and see if pdflatex is available to compile it.\n\nWriting the paper... for a thorough but \"够审\" quality paper.\n\nI'm noticing the CF violation rates: SciERC has 9.9% of entities with cross-field issues, DocRED only 2.57%, but Llama's DocRED jumps to 12.02% — so the model actually introduces more violations than the original dataset. This is worth highlighting.\n\nNow I need to map out all 18 experiments across the paper sections: the violation landscape comparisons in §3, the main SciERC and DocRED results with different constraint levels in §5.1-5.2, the cross-model experiments with Llama in §5.3, and the post-hoc baseline comparison in §5.4. Let me structure the full paper around these.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12400,"cache_read_input_tokens":23218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12400},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6dfc5dc4-a95d-4cb7-b790-c6ab597d3a86","uuid":"580690b1-c400-465c-b6c1-1f91755ad2b9"}
